cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Kurt, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Kurt: a proof language with an automatic checker"
abstract: >-
  Kurt is a small language for writing mathematical proofs in a form close to how people write
  them, and a checker that tells you immediately, line by line, whether each step follows. It is
  meant for students learning to prove things.
authors:
  - family-names: Harmeling
    given-names: Stefan
    affiliation: TU Dortmund
version: 0.7.3
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
url: "https://www.kurt-lang.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/harmeling/kurt-lang"
keywords:
  - proof checker
  - logic
  - mathematics education
  - natural deduction
